  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U4", "U24"],
      "pins": ["U4.4", "U4.5", "U24.4", "U24.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "The isolated CAN transceivers U4 and U24 have both GND1 and GND2 pins connected to the common GND net.",
      "expected": "For an isolated CAN transceiver, GND1 (logic side) and GND2 (bus side) should be separate grounds to preserve galvanic isolation; the specification states the board has isolated CAN buses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"53\") (name \"GND\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U24\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`) ... through an isolated CAN transceiver"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The intended CAN isolation is defeated; bus-side grounds are tied to logic ground, allowing ground loops and removing the isolation protection.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["SW5", "R28", "R83", "U4", "U24"],
      "pins": ["SW5.1", "SW5.2", "SW5.3", "SW5.4", "R28.2", "R83.2", "U4.6", "U4.7", "U24.6", "U24.7"],
      "nets": ["/NET0075", "/NET0078", "/NET0022", "/NET0209", "Net-(R28-Pad2)", "Net-(R83-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "SW5 is a 2-bit SPST DIP switch. R28 (120 Ω) from U24 CANL is tied to SW5.1, R83 (120 Ω) from U4 CANL to SW5.2, U4 CANH to SW5.3, and U24 CANH to SW5.4. With the standard SW_DIP_x02 pairing (1-3 and 2-4), closing SW5 connects U24 CANL to U4 CANH and U4 CANL to U24 CANH, cross-terminating/bridging the two CAN buses.",
      "expected": "Switchable CAN termination should connect each 120 Ω resistor between CANH and CANL of the same bus without coupling or shorting the two separate CAN buses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"SW5\") (value \"SW_DIP_x02\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(libpart (lib \"Switch\") (part \"SW_DIP_x02\") (description \"2x DIP Switch, Single Pole Single Throw (SPST) switch, small symbol\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"195\") (name \"Net-(R28-Pad2)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R28\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"SW5\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"Pin_1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"46\") (name \"/NET0209\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"SW5\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"Pin_3\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"CANH\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If SW5 is closed for termination, the two CAN buses are improperly loaded and coupled rather than correctly terminated, likely causing CAN communication errors or bus conflicts.",
      "confidence": 0.78
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["Q9"],
      "pins": ["Q9.3"],
      "nets": [],
      "observed": "Q9 is an N-MOSFET low-side switch with its gate driven from GPIO4 through R101 and its source tied to GND, but its drain pin (Q9.3) does not appear in any net.",
      "expected": "A populated MOSFET switch should have its drain connected to the intended load/output, or it should be marked DNP/removed if unused.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"Q9\") (value \"Q_NMOS_GSD\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"Q9\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\") (pintype \"input\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"Q9\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(pin (num \"3\") (name \"D\") (type \"passive\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "GPIO4 controls a MOSFET with a floating drain, so this switched output is non-functional; if Q9 was intended to drive an actuator or power path, that function is missing.",
      "confidence": 0.62
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain at least two strong CAN-related deviations: the isolated CAN transceivers have their separate grounds tied to common GND, and the CAN termination DIP switch is cross-wired between the two buses. A third likely issue is Q9, whose gate is driven but whose drain is unconnected."
}

